From: SamiEnazi <85966743+SamiEnazi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] the engine exe and the game module (slim split, 2026-11-14)

The exe no longer links the lift: the lifted PPU/SPU code and the lifted firmware are the
game module (Infamous2Game.dll / libInfamous2Game.so), built on the player's PC by
tools/build_module.py with clang + lld only, and bound at the start of main
(engine/include/ps3emu/ps3_module.h). This patch:
- CMakeLists.txt: the exe from the port's and the engine's own sources only, against the
  engine's ppu_recomp.h (tools/ppu_engine_header.py: no lifted prototype); every engine TU
  force-includes runtime/module/ps3_module_vars.h; Linux exports the engine's functions to
  the module (-rdynamic).
- main.cpp: ps3_module_attach() first (a missing or mismatched module = a message, exit 3);
  ps3_module_sync() once vm_base is set; PS3_PGO_DUMP_AT writes an instrumented module's
  counters.
- gpu_light.c, gpu_ssao.c: the light / SSAO jobs' lifted routines found by (image, LS
  address) in the SPU registry (spu_find_function), no longer linked by name.

